Unlimited items makes the game trivial, since much of the game is based
on the scarcity of certain items (helpful rings, spellbooks, etc. that
would otherwise be worth a wish).

Unlimited score makes the high score table worthless. Both
exceptionally high and exceptionally low scores should be impressive,
but as it stands now, exceptionally high scores requires very little
skill (in terms of gameplay and problem solving) to accomplish. They
still require some skill, to be sure, but not an amount of skill that's
in any way correlated with the scores they can achieve.

Finally, if you take away the unlimited items and the unlimited score,
why would farming need to exist? Who would go to the trouble of farming
for no actual benefit?

